[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3470819324","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112228#issuecomment-3470819324","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112228","id":3470819324,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7O4H_8","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-31T00:30:11Z","updated_at":"2025-10-31T00:30:11Z","body":"The issue is coming from your code. \n\nSpecifically this:\n\n```\nvec2 uv_quantised = floor(UV / 0.05);\nfloat checker = clamp(mod(uv_quantised.x + uv_quantised.y, 2.0), 0.0, 1.0);\nchecker = step(1.0, checker);\n```\n\nParticularly what is happening is you creating a discontinuity/seam by quantizing the uv and checker pattern. Therefore, you create a massive jump in the first order derivative of the normal. When using the `texture` function to sample from a texture, the GPU will use the first order derivative to decide what mipmap level to read from. Because you create that discontinuity, the GPU will sample from a very high mip level on the seam and create the artifacts that you have there. \n\nThe Screen Space Roughness Limiter is designed to help reduce this form of aliasing, but it can only do so much. \n\nIn general when programming shaders you need to avoid sharp discontinuities, or you need to avoid relying on derivatives (i.e. no using `texture`, use `textureLOD` instead). In your case, since the `texture` call is done internally, you should avoid using the WorldEnvironment Sky, and instead use a custom `RADIANCE` and `IRRADIANCE` in your shader (or use continuous normals)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3470819324/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3471849073","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112228#issuecomment-3471849073","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112228","id":3471849073,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7O8DZx","user":{"login":"liljohn360","id":8534384,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MzQzODQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8534384?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360","html_url":"https://github.com/liljohn360","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liljohn360/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-31T08:30:01Z","updated_at":"2025-10-31T08:30:01Z","body":"Thanks for the nudge in the right direction!\n\nSince I can’t use ReflectionProbe with a custom RADIANCE, I’ll look into compiling Godot with textureLOD instead!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3471849073/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]